Subject: Cantor Phase3 Topology Acquisition Lineage Forms Plan

& [PlanIdentity] is exact
  + [plan_uuid] is df4f8a03-7bf7-42f0-b15b-d3131d5607b2
  + [source_snapshot_uuid] is 6fffb113-5add-4910-970a-08ad7b82f0ec
  + [requirements] are P3TALF-001 through P3TALF-014
  + [state] is planned_unsigned

& [Step01_PreserveAndAudit] is complete
  + preserve exact source, source manifest, and processing manifest
  + bind selection, current scanner formation, machine and topology forms, carrier authorities, source modules, and physical gates
  + decide producer-admission deferral and source-revision need before explosion

& [Step02_DelineateExplodeRefine] is complete
  + separate claim, validation, derivation, output-only result, production admission, evidence issuance, receipt issuance, and physical truth
  + atomize P3TALF-001 through P3TALF-014 with verification and rejection routes
  + refine twenty material terms and ten forbidden substitutions

& [Step03_ConstrainPruneAndThreatReview] is complete
  + independently extract and reapply C01 through C24
  + prune fourteen speculative surfaces and retain eight bounded proof structures
  + deny fourteen provenance, identity, scope, order, serde, fixture, resource, and authority threats
  + stop on collision, ambiguity, or source-revision requirement

& [Step04_ExhaustAndDesignData] is complete
  + run seven identity, language, provenance, ownership, fault, effect, and evolution folds
  + close the conceptual type graph, structural scope, two-lineage cardinality, validation order, faults, resources, versioning, and provenance
  + retain implementation and every effect authority absent

& [Step05_RegisterSupport] is complete as unsigned formation
  + create justification, this plan, retrieval registry, fourteen-requirement matrix, and bounded build slice
  + map every requirement to source, SJS support, proof route, refusal, and authority state

& [Step06_Canonicalize] is required
  + create one separate canonical profile 0.1 without editing prior source or SJS intermediates
  + fix exact public claim types, output-only result, validation order, fault vocabulary, nonclaims, and production-admission absence
  + bind exact current nested profiles, modules, signatures, and hashes

& [Step07_ArtifactPhaseLockAndSign] is required
  + recompute source and every derived artifact hash after canonical content is final
  + reapply P3TALF-001 through P3TALF-014, C01 through C24, T01 through T14, and all seven folds
  + issue one exact satisfaction signature only if no requirement, constraint, or authority boundary is unresolved
  + state exact permitted one-module zero-effect implementation diff and every denied capability

& [Step08_ImplementOnlyIfSigned] is conditional
  + add at most one safe pure cantor_ecosystem module and one lib export
  + reuse current serde, form, assembly, digest, and reconciliation surfaces without dependency change
  + implement strict claims, deterministic validation, current rederivation, ClaimOnly result, and bounded faults
  + do not add producer admission, Windows calls, clocks, receipt conversion, issuer, consumer, fixture execution, or effects

& [Step09_VerifyAndPublish] is conditional after implementation
  + run focused adversarial and static tests in debug and overflow-checked release
  + run full locked offline workspace gates, warnings-denied Clippy, format, scripts, recursive evidence, provenance, rollback, and attribution checks
  + publish only source-bound code and intentional transitive manifests
  + replay exact gates after push and prove local-upstream equality and clean tracked tree

& [Rollback] is monotonic
  + before signature remove derived unsigned formation artifacts while preserving source and prior SJS provenance
  + after signature invalidate the exact signature and derived authority without changing source or historical evidence
  + after pure implementation revert only the one module, export, tests, and direct proof artifacts
  + no physical or persisted runtime state exists to reverse

& [StopRules] are fail closed
  + stop on source, profile, module, signature, or carrier drift
  + stop on incomplete scope or lineage, duplicate identity, invalid causal edge, current rederivation fault, Different, or unsupported evidence grade
  + stop on claim-to-provenance, Equal-to-physical-evidence, output-to-receipt, or fixture-to-production promotion
  + stop on dependency, Cargo, unsafe, platform, filesystem, clock, random, process, environment, network, persistence, model, tool, acquisition, issuer, consumer, mutation, seal, neural, distributed, FPGA, or Minecraft surface
  + stop before any M2C physical implementation until separate preserved source, SJS, signature, and host proof exist
